se,"pull":true}},"body":"Sorry I don't know well this library and its code but I confused about the different behaviors (depending on the operating system) concerning the empty constructor for `glm::mat4()`.\r\n\r\nOn my personal desktop with Debian 9.3 (as well as Ubuntu 16.04) it returns the identity matrix (what I was expected) but in Travis-CI for Darwin (OS-X) returns a matrix filled with 0 and I think this is not the expected behavior. Maybe I'm wrong but the init seems to depend on macro GLM_FORCE_CTOR_INIT and therefore can give different behavior depending on homebrew and apt-get. \r\n\r\nHere extracts of the log:\r\n\r\nHomebrew:\r\n```\r\n==> Downloading https://homebrew.bintray.com/bottles/glm-0.9.9.0.sierra.bottle.tar.gz\r\n==> Pouring glm-0.9.9.0.sierra.bottle.tar.gz\r\n```\r\n\r\nClang version:\r\n```\r\nApple LLVM version 8.1.0 (clang-802.0.42)\r\nTarget: x86_64-apple-darwin16.7.0\r\nThread model: posix\r\nInstalledDir: /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Toolchains/XcodeDefault.xctoolchain/usr/bin\r\n```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/792/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/792/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]